  "illustration_prompt": "Create a single publication-quality landscape 3:2 narrative illustration for an adult illustrated English-reading booklet. Finished standalone artwork, not a book mockup, not a collage of multiple unrelated panels. Sophisticated contemporary editorial gouache and watercolor, carefully controlled colored-pencil accents, velvety matte paint, subtle warm paper texture, soft natural daylight. Warm ivory paper dominates; subdued eucalyptus and sage greens structure the composition; restrained buttery lemon-yellow and dusty terracotta accents. Calm, comfortable, refined, credible drawing and natural anatomy. An airy coherent composition with one clear story focal point and at most two supporting details, generous breathing room at all edges and softly feathered painted edges into ivory. Detailed but uncluttered. Historically and scientifically appropriate objects, clothing and setting. Show the particular article's pivotal event or mechanism rather than a generic portrait or generic textbook symbols. Human figures treated with dignity; no grotesque caricature, no sensational violence or visible injuries. For disasters, emphasize the setting, evidence or human response without graphic suffering. For uncertain scientific claims, depict the observations and investigation without presenting debated mechanisms as proven. Absolutely no typography, captions, letters, numbers, logos, watermarks, diagram labels, fake writing or invented charts anywhere. Do not render invisible forces as literal magic. Avoid corporate vector icons, slick 3D rendering and childish cartoon style. High-quality, print-ready visual storytelling, matching a warm ivory-and-sage adult watercolor booklet.\n\nARTICLE-SPECIFIC SCENE: A quiet field-observation scene in the Chernobyl exclusion zone: one realistic wild boar walks across the edge of an abandoned rural lane, while a small unmarked wildlife camera trap strapped to a foreground tree records it. The old Soviet-era farmhouse beyond is subdued and partly overgrown, suggesting human absence, not an idyllic untouched Eden. Fallen brown leaves remain clearly visible on the ground as a supporting detail. Scientifically restrained: no glowing radiation, no mutant creatures, no suggestion that abundant wildlife proves health or safety. Camera trapping and a single observable animal are the visual story, not a claim of universal ecological recovery. Soft sage vegetation, ivory misty sky, restrained terracotta leaves, calm dignified wildlife anatomy.",
